Subject: [PATCH] support: unlink failed event, timer, idle and signal sources

Base: PipeWire 1.6.11, 4287f31510771fc999f8a58a024c81ca10b8d55f
Apply after 0001 and 0002.

These four source constructors use the same get_source path as loop_add_io:
the allocation is already on source_list before fd creation/poll registration.
Unlink it before freeing on either failure. Preserve their existing owned-fd
close/error behavior and do not change successful source registration.

This completes the source-list correction in 0001 for the cancellation and
first-frame timer directly used by the capture worker, plus the identical idle
and signal constructors. The pinned source blob is
e5e49849fe84955a63a534d4f008ca84d4e6b3fb. The same missing unlink was found in
upstream 685cb07a92acac24677fded669308f036207bb9a; no corresponding upstream
change was found to reuse. The original MIT notices continue to apply.
This is a huhucapture adaptation, not an assertion of upstream acceptance.

diff --git a/spa/plugins/support/loop.c b/spa/plugins/support/loop.c
--- a/spa/plugins/support/loop.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/support/loop.c
@@ -984,6 +984,7 @@
 error_exit_close:
 	spa_system_close(impl->system, source->source.fd);
 error_exit_free:
+	spa_list_remove(&source->link);
 	free(source);
 	errno = -res;
 error_exit:
@@ -1034,6 +1035,7 @@
 error_exit_close:
 	spa_system_close(impl->system, source->source.fd);
 error_exit_free:
+	spa_list_remove(&source->link);
 	free(source);
 	errno = -res;
 error_exit:
@@ -1100,6 +1102,7 @@
 error_exit_close:
 	spa_system_close(impl->system, source->source.fd);
 error_exit_free:
+	spa_list_remove(&source->link);
 	free(source);
 	errno = -res;
 error_exit:
@@ -1181,6 +1184,7 @@
